# watch.items — the PR/issue items a reasonix session watches through the
# harness-INDEPENDENT watcher, `marketplace/scripts/gh_watch.sh`.
#
# One item per line: `owner/repo#num`, `owner/repo/pull/num`,
# `owner/repo/issues/num`, or a full https://github.com/owner/repo/(pull|issues)/num
# URL. Blank lines and lines starting with `#` are ignored. This is the SAME
# grammar `.opencode/pr-watch.items` uses and the same grammar the watcher
# parses, so an item list is portable between harnesses.
#
# This shipped file is comment-only, so the watcher is INERT by default.
# Uncomment (or add) a line below to arm it, then start a new reasonix session
# (the SessionStart hook in `.reasonix/settings.json` reads this file).
#
# WHY A SHELL WATCHER AND NOT A PLUGIN. The watcher is deliberately NOT a
# reasonix code extension: `gh_watch.sh` is harness-independent, already carries
# the rate-limit discipline (one batched GraphQL poll per interval - 300s by default - a free
# /rate_limit guard, a 300s poll floor), the stall alarm, and `--auto-rearm`.
# Wrapping it in a sidecar would duplicate that logic in a second place. The
# SessionStart hook below only ARMS it.
#
# WHY NOT `[progress_watch]`. That block (in `reasonix.toml`) is the in-session
# LOOP guard: it detects a model repeating itself and can pause or retry. It
# cannot see a GitHub PR. The two are different mechanisms and both are wanted.
#
# acme/widget#12
